class resign_crypt {
public $CYPHER = 'rijndael-128';
public $MODE = 'cfb';
public $SALT = 'test';

public function __construct($CYPHER = null, $MODE = null, $SALT = null) {
    if ($CYPHER) {
        $this->CYPHER = $CYPHER;
    }
    if ($MODE) {
        $this->MODE = $MODE;
    }
    if ($SALT) {
        $this->SALT = $SALT;
    }
}

public function encryptMcrypt($plaintext, $password = '', $compress = true) {
    if ($compress) {
        $plaintext = gzdeflate($plaintext);
    }
    $td = mcrypt_module_open($this->CYPHER, '', $this->MODE, '');
    $iv = mcrypt_create_iv(mcrypt_enc_get_iv_size($td), MCRYPT_RAND);
    $key = $this->SALT . trim($password);
    mcrypt_generic_init($td, $key, $iv);
    $crypttext = mcrypt_generic($td, $plaintext);
    mcrypt_generic_deinit($td);
    $crypttext = $iv . $crypttext;
    return $crypttext;
}

public function decryptMcrypt($crypttext, $password = '', $decompress = true) {
    $td = mcrypt_module_open($this->CYPHER, '', $this->MODE, '');
    $ivsize = mcrypt_enc_get_iv_size($td);
    $iv = substr($crypttext, 0, $ivsize);
    $crypttext = substr($crypttext, $ivsize);
    $key = $this->SALT . trim($password);
    mcrypt_generic_init($td, $key, $iv);
    $plaintext = mdecrypt_generic($td, $crypttext);
    if ($decompress) {
        $plaintext = gzinflate($plaintext);
    }
    return $plaintext;
}
}
```
The Resign Crypt class takes three parameters:
1. `$CYPHER`: The name of the cryptographic algorithm to use. In this case, we've used the Rijndael-128 algorithm.
2. `$MODE`: The mode of operation for the encryption algorithm. In this case, we've used the CFB (Cipher Feedback) mode.
3. `$SALT`: A secret key that is used to encrypt and decrypt the data. In this case, we've used the string 'test'.
The `encryptMcrypt` function takes a plaintext string, a password (if any), and a boolean flag indicating whether to compress the output. If the output is compressed, it uses the `gzdeflate` function to compress it.
The `decryptMcrypt` function takes a crypttext string, a password (if any), and a boolean flag indicating whether to decompress the output. If the output is decompressed, it uses the `gzinflate` function to decompress it.
The encryption and decryption functions use the Mcrypt module to perform the actual encryption and decryption. The Mcrypt module is a CRYPTOAPI library that provides encryption and decryption functions for various encryption algorithms, including RC2, DES, and Triple DES.

