Creating a React Hook to check the maximum possible video resolution in the webcam involves utilizing the `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia()` API, which allows access to device media input and output. This hook will return the highest available video resolution of the user's webcam.

Here's a basic implementation of the hook:
```javascript
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const useMaxVideoResolution = () => {
  const [maxResolution, setMaxResolution] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const getVideoStream = async () => {
      const stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ video: true });
      const videoElement = document.createElement('video');
      videoElement.srcObject = stream;
      videoElement.onloadedmetadata = () => {
        const videoTracks = stream.getVideoTracks();
        const capabilities = videoTracks[0].getCapabilities();
        setMaxResolution({ width: capabilities.width.max, height: capabilities.height.max });
        stream.getTracks().forEach((track) => track.stop());
      };
      document.body.appendChild(videoElement);
    };

    getVideoStream();

    return () => {
      setMaxResolution(null);
    };
  }, []);

  return maxResolution;
};
```
To use this hook in a functional component, you would do:
```javascript
