Changing the session name in Vtiger CRM API with React Native involves several steps and requires some understanding of how APIs work and how to make HTTP requests in React Native. Here is a step-by-step guide:

1. Install Axios: Axios is a promise-based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js that lets you send HTTP requests. You can use it to make requests to the Vtiger API.
You can install Axios using npm, follow these steps:
```astro
npm install axios
```
or
```csharp
yarn add axios
```
2. Use Axios to send a POST request to the Vtiger API:

First, create a new JavaScript file called `index.js` in your React Native project:
```javascript
import axios from 'axios';

export default {
  updateSession(sessionName) {
    const url = 'https://your-vtiger-domain.com/crm/mobileapi/ Session_Manager/api/v1/session';
    const headers = {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'Accept': 'application/json',
    };
    const data = { sessionName };
    return axios.post(url, data, { headers })
      .then(res => {
        console.log(res);
      })
      .catch(err => {
        console.log(err);
      });
  },
};
```
3. In your React Native component, use the `updateSession` function to change the session name:

Make sure you have imported `index` from the new module:
```javascript
import index from '../path/to/your/index';

// usage:
index.updateSession('new_session_name');
```
This will send a POST request to the Vtiger API to change the session name. Note that you need to replace "https://your-vtiger-domain.com/crm/mobileapi/ Session_Manager/api/v1/session" with your actual Vtiger CRM URL.
4. Handle any errors that might occur: Axios will reject the promise with an error if the request fails. Be sure to handle it with a `.catch()` block, as shown in the example above.

Please note that this example assumes that you have a valid Vtiger CRM account with an active session. Also, update the URL, headers, and the session name before making the request. If you're using a localhost VTiger instance, use the URL `http://localhost:port/vtiger/crm/mobileapi` instead.

